[Music]  this morning on the dish one of la's new  hot spots mother tongue launched by chef  michael mina the cuisine is a reflection  of the private fitness club it sits  above to lead the kitchen and help  create the menu mina tapped fernando  darine as executive chef whose interest  in yoga and clean eating made him the  perfect choice for what mother tongue  has named a new culinary dialect  it doesn't feel like a  traditional restaurant nourishing the  mind and the body that's the intent of  mother tongue the patio here is probably  my favorite executive chef fernando  darine says it's a concept built into  the restaurant which occupies the top  floor of the social and fitness club  highmat a name that means the feeling of  home the name of the restaurant mother  tongue was a very easy reflection of  what highmat is we wanted to take  all these dishes  from around the world  and transforming it into our own mother  tongue  simply put it's comfort food from around  the world but all made using nutritional  ingredients without sacrificing taste  a challenge chef fernando as he's known  at mother tongue embraced i took this  project because of the challenge and  because this reflects  my lifestyle as well i like to eat clean  i like to cook clean and the food that  it's on that menu is a reflection of  that take mother tongue's version of a  traditional bread service pita alongside  three colorful and flavorful dips you  can mix the colors and you can make a  painting if you like there's a syrian  based walnut mahamura  i love this one a beet hummus and an  avocado and tarragon mousse with the  antioxidant spirulina on top they all  have like very distinct flavors but like  they got your mouth  going along with health there's also a  focus on sustainability like in the  mother tongue lamb we use a not so  popular cut the neck which is very  flavorful and a very sustainable thing  cured for two days roasted for five to  six hours then shredded before being  served 