it's very similar i'm even thinking in a  recipe it's like i need a little more  violin or i need a little more spice i  use that a lot yeah that analogy i say  this needs a little eq  like a little bit more base or a little  bit more uh lids  fats and oils yeah are like the base  and highs vinegars and lemon  the right combination  harmony something mother tongue strives  for in each item on the menu oh my gosh  it's ever popular rizzoni a perfect  example orzo corn puree and strachatella  cheese with black truffle shaved on top  it's a very simple dish but i honestly  think that simplicity is the ultimate  sophistication another mother tongue  mantra played out in dessert  this yeah  [Music]  this is wonderful  which for us was an indian inspired  carrot cake pudding with cardamom cream  and pistachios i'm going to go back to  the menu because we started talking  about the challenge of creating it but  how much fun did you have in creating  the menu it's probably the most fun part  of opening a restaurant i like to go and  i like to watch the table it can be a  sounds a little creepy  sounds a little creepy but i don't do  that often but i like to see you know  people's reactions and probably the most  interesting  reaction that i ever got in my cooking  career really because i feel like here i  was able to translate my personality to  its fullest  to the menu and people acknowledge when  something is true you know something's  not fake the menu here is  truthful to what i am  as is the beverage menu we talk about  that health and all of that the balance  it's there too even with like spiked  kombuchas this is their bourbon bee one  thing i want to point out chef fernando  practices yoga and that balance he and i  talked about that you find in yoga is  something he brings to the kitchen as  well you feel all of it in that  restaurant love it chance hit hollywood  he knows a guy i want that dessert

